      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تصبّح</span></b>  <i>He slept in the morning;</i> or <i>first
part of day, before sunrise.</i> (S, Msb, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
And <i>He ate such food as is termed a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صُبْحَة</span>.
(K, TA.) It is said in a trad., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْ تَصَبَّحَ بِسَبْعِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَرَاتِ عَجْوَةٍ</span> [<i>He who eats as a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صُبْحَة</span> <i>seven dates
of the sort called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَجْوَة</span>]. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also 8, in
two places.

